{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "model": "SidecarLifetime",
  "assumptions": [
    "One parent row and one external attribute have exactly two immutable chunk parts per external value.",
    "Each parent and chunk MVCC identifier maps to a transaction family; root and nested identifiers of one family share own-write visibility.",
    "The second writer waits for the exclusive parent row lock and, after acquiring it, selects the current committed row.",
    "A writer may observe its own row only between statement actions and after each complete statement or savepoint rollback.",
    "Other readers may observe committed versions after any individual physical statement or undo effect.",
    "One old reader snapshot begins at commit epoch zero; the model closes it at most once.",
    "Requested values are materialized before a reentrant same-transaction mutation, or their operation-scoped view is discarded.",
    "Starting rollback or commit invalidates a lazy operation-scoped view without requiring allocation; returned materialized bytes remain owned.",
    "A fresh ID is never reissued, including after rollback, and unchanged updates retain their existing ID.",
    "The model abstracts physical slot reuse, indexes, crash recovery, WAL and history into separate obligations.",
    "Statement and savepoint expectations are captured outside the physical undo journal, and a completed rollback restores that captured prefix.",
    "After the finite workload and snapshot release, weakly fair collection eventually removes each eligible committed deletion."
  ],
